    "created_at": "2016-03-21T13:09:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-21T13:09:27Z",
    "body": "It seems like a big plus with dictionaries that the members are evaluated immediately, but are there reasons to ever prefer the \"lazy\" behavior of callback interfaces?\n\nIt looks within reach to limit callback interfaces to the three existing cases, which are all single-function cases.\n",
