    "created_at": "2018-02-14T13:29:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-02-14T13:29:14Z",
    "body": "Is it really true that getter/setter is \"legacy\" and discouraged in new APIs?  Can anyone provide a reference for this documenting the extent of the consensus here?  In the absence of agreed upon guidance (eg. captured concretely in the webidl spec), I'm personally not willing to block requests to ship such new APIs in blink (such as [Typed OM](https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/d/msg/blink-dev/6ai8np0DSOA/XJak-Nw0AgAJ)).\r\n\r\n/cc @ajklein @foolip @chrishtr",
