    "created_at": "2018-02-14T14:39:02Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-02-14T14:39:02Z",
    "body": "I think there is general agreement that named getters/setters are a bad idea.\r\n\r\nFor indexed getters/setters, things are complicated, not least because there are legitimate use cases that have no other solutions right now.  Indexed setters do require some careful spec prose around out-of-bounds sets.",
